{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And you shall not go up by steps.</b> When you build a ramp for the altar you shall not make it step by step — אשקלו״נש בְּלַעַז — rather it shall be smooth and sloping." "<b>That your nakedness not be exposed.</b> For by means of steps you must widen your strides; and even though it is not actual exposure of nakedness — since it is written ״וַעֲשֵׂה לָהֶם מִכְנְסֵי בָד״ — nevertheless widening the strides is close to exposure of nakedness, and you would be treating them with disrespect; and this is a קַ״וָ — if these stones, which have no awareness to object to their disgrace, the Torah said: since they are needed, do not treat them with disrespect — then your fellow, who is in the image of your Creator and does object to his disgrace, all the more so!"], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French escalier, 'stairs'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:23.693211109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}